e/up to bf16 pre-elementwise; a fused kernel is *more* accurate), fp32 accumulators required, fp32 result buffer + final bf16 cast. `N=4096` (atol 0.0076) is the numeric **canary**.\n\n**Triton design space:** Option A padded-batch two-kernel (correctness-first baseline) → Option B sorted-token grouped GEMM (vLLM `fused_moe` style, on-the-fly gather, de-padding); Option C single megakernel rejected (smem blowup); split-K deferred.\n\n**Validation:** the only correctness signal is `evaluate_candidate.sh feedback` (1 eval = 5 workloads, counts against 100-eval budget); no local harness allowed, so correctness is engineered up-front by reusing reference metadata, and candidates change one thing at a time.\n\nStopping here as instructed — no `docs/plan.md` and no solution code created."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"139cd17e-87be-401b-b89f-996c3aab37c1","uuid":"1a480d26-f293-4800-bf73-aeb2a69334ae","timestamp":"2026-09-16T14:48:52.725Z"}
