(Option B) → `c004` `num_stages` → `c005` tile/warp geometry → `c006` L2 expert grouping, plus conditional `c007` bf16-round canary fix and named fallback branches (c002a/c003a).\n- **§3 Correctness checks** — engineered up front since the only sanctioned signal is `evaluate_candidate.sh feedback` (one eval = all 5); includes a failure-triage table (all-5 vs canary-only vs single-shape).\n- **§4 Performance hypotheses** — per-lever mechanism/expected effect, realistic ~1.1–1.3× geomean ceiling.\n- **§5 Decision rules** — accept/neutral/reject thresholds (±2% noise band) with attributability.\n- **§6 Stopping criteria** — convergence, design exhaustion, budget; `SEARCH_COMPLETE` on stop; never run `final` without operator approval.\n- **§7 Evidence format** — full append-only `candidates.jsonl` schema (parent, source hash, hypothesis, per-workload results, geomean, decision, cumulative evals, skill usage) with transcription rules.\n- **§8 Skill usage** and **§9 execution checklist**.\n\nNo code was written and no candidate was evaluated, per the workflow. Ready to implement `c001` on your go-ahead.","ttft_ms":5483,"ttft_stream_ms":5482,"time_to_request_ms":58,"type":"result","duration_ms":268338,"uuid":"545b72f2-2617-4516-9ec7-f07dbdd4a2cf"}
